Inquisitor Penitence is an Inquisitor of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]]. He is tall, and his raiment is identical to every other Inquisitor's, where raiments are usually a little different for each person. Where [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Brother Zeal|Brother Zeal]] has pearlescent writing on his forehead, Penitence has the same mother-of-pearl material worked into tattoos on his forearms. When he takes notes, his writing flows off of his arm and onto the page. He gives away almost nothing, and his expression is hard to read.

He questions people in a room below the lobby, at a plain metal table under a single light, where a golden bell rings whenever a true thing is said. He has taken over the matter of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove|Heart]] and the radar dish from the Party, and will pass nothing of it to anyone outside the Inquisition, even Cardinal Weatherhead.
